  "//": "The reviewed git-relay seat policy (README, Policy).  seat_policy.py renders it into GIT_RELAY_SEATS_JSON and installs it on the relay host.  Every seat signs in with its own admin-minted ST-MCP bearer (auth shared) and acts as its own GitHub App, so no entry holds a token.  The App slug of each identity is the swu- App whose GitHub description names that seat;  five are not swu-<identity>:  MA is swu-rob, GROK is swu-grok-build, MM is swu-minimax, JET-CHAT is swu-jet, AMP is swu-amp-agent (swu-amp is reserved for an account).  JET-CHAT is the full Jet login on swu-jet; the original JET connection is wake-only and has no Git entry (Q7).  AMP signs in with its own bearer and acts as its own swu-amp-agent App.  Repositories: 2026-11-01 every-repo widening:  every active seat reaches Simple-With-Us/* and jaywedgeworth22/* - the two verified namespaces - via the owner/* form the relay engine already matches;  the 18-repo fleet list and Echo's narrower set are retired.  Capabilities mirror the host's reviewed live rollout exactly:  each active seat carries the live 175-action list (the 7 existing relay actions plus the 168-workflow rollout) and the live 10-key mint ceiling;  the retired BF-BUILDER pin holds its live 27-action list and 6-key ceiling (no workflows).  swu-amp-agent and swu-wise keep the host's exact live action ordering through their own pinned profiles (same set, ceiling and repositories as fleet).  Identity, rate and review gates are unchanged.",
